            <ArticleTitle>Eyelid apraxia associated with deep brain stimulation of the periaqueductal gray area.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1652-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jocn.2014.03.002</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0967-5868(14)00107-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a patient with eyelid apraxia following deep brain stimulation of the periaqueductal gray area. Based on the position of our electrode, we argue that the phenomenon is linked to inhibition of the nearby central caudal nucleus of the oculomotor nucleus by high frequency stimulation.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Published by Elsevier Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
